Rule 1 (inputs must be broadcast-compatible)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) ≥ ndim(v_2) then (∀k ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : if k < ndim(v_1) - ndim(v_2) then true else shape(v_1, k) = shape(v_2, k - (ndim(v_1) - ndim(v_2))) ∨ shape(v_1, k) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, k - (ndim(v_1) - ndim(v_2))) = 1) else (∀k ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : if k < ndim(v_2) - ndim(v_1) then true else shape(v_2, k) = shape(v_1, k - (ndim(v_2) - ndim(v_1))) ∨ shape(v_2, k) = 1 ∨ shape(v_1, k - (ndim(v_2) - ndim(v_1))) = 1)
>>
Rule 2 (when ranks are equal, each axis must be pairwise broadcastable)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) then (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i) ∨ shape(v_1, i) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, i) = 1)
