Rule 3 (x1 and x2 must be broadcastable: v1-aligned condition)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : if i - (ndim(v_1) - ndim(v_2)) ≥ 0 then (shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i - (ndim(v_1) - ndim(v_2))) ∨ shape(v_1, i) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, i - (ndim(v_1) - ndim(v_2))) = 1)
>>
Rule 4 (x1 and x2 must be broadcastable: v2-aligned condition)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : if i - (ndim(v_2) - ndim(v_1)) ≥ 0 then (shape(v_2, i) = shape(v_1, i - (ndim(v_2) - ndim(v_1))) ∨ shape(v_2, i) = 1 ∨ shape(v_1, i - (ndim(v_2) - ndim(v_1))) = 1)
>>
Rule 5 (when ranks match, each dimension must be equal or 1 for broadcasting)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i) ∨ shape(v_1, i) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, i) = 1
